ect is concluded to be robust across thresholds, with larger effects at more liberal definitions of \"dark\"", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["threshold sensitivity"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 114, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[131, 131]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 115, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[132, 132]], "note": "subsection 4.3 heading"}, {"id": 116, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[133, 133]], "assertion": "only the most extreme skin-tone categories (0.0 vs 1.0) were compared", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["extreme groups"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 117, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[134, 136]], "assertion": "very light (0.0) has a 1.11% red card rate (n=33,723), very dark (1.0) has 1.41% (n=7,570), raw difference 0.30pp", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["extreme groups", "red card rate"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 118, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[137, 137]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 119, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[138, 138]], "assertion": "the effect is concluded to be even more pronounced at the extremes, supporting the hypothesis", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["extreme groups"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 120, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[139, 139]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 121, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[140, 140]], "note": "subsection 4.4 heading"}, {"id": 122, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[141, 141]], "assertion": "key confounders showed expected effects in the model", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confounders"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 123, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[142, 146]], "assertion": "confounder effects found: games OR=1.13/game (p<0.001); yellow cards OR=1.09/card (p<0.001); Center Back OR=1.82 (p<0.001); France league OR=1.65 (p<0.001); Spain league OR=1.62 (p<0.001)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["games", "yellow cards", "player position", "league"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 124, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[147, 147]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 125, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[148, 148]], "assertion": "the skin tone effect persists after adjustment despite these strong confounders", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["skin tone effect"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 126, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[149, 151]], "note": "blank + divider + blank"}, {"id": 127, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[152, 152]], "note": "section 5 heading"}, {"id": 128, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[153, 153]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 129, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[154, 154]], "note": "subsection 5.1 heading"}, {"id": 130, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[155, 155]], "assertion": "14.66% of dyads were excluded due to missing skin tone ratings (no player photo)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["exclusions"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 131, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[156, 156]], "assertion": "missing data may not be random since excluded dyads have lower red card rates", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["missing data"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 132, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[157, 157]], "note": "caveat about possible bias direction from exclusions, no specific action asserted"}, {"id": 133, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[158, 158]], "assertion": "the sample is still considered large (124,621 dyads) and represents 77% of players with photos, as mitigation for the missing-data concern", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sample size"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 134, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[159, 159]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 135, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[160, 160]], "note": "subsection 5.2 heading"}, {"id": 136, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[161, 161]], "note": "general caveat that causation cannot be established"}, {"id": 137, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[162, 162]], "note": "potential unmeasured confounders label"}, {"id": 138, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[163, 167]], "note": "speculative list of potential unmeasured confounders, no specific action"}, {"id": 139, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[168, 168]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 140, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[169, 169]], "note": "subsection 5.3 heading"}, {"id": 141, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[170, 170]], "assertion": "skin tone coding was based on still photos, subject to rater interpretation and photo quality/lighting", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["skin tone coding"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 142, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[171, 171]], "assertion": "inter-rater reliability was excellent (r=0.923), restated as offsetting the measurement concern", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["inter-rater reliability"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 143, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[172, 172]], "assertion": "red cards capture only the most severe sanctions", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["red cards"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [144]}, {"id": 144, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[172, 172]], "assertion": "yellow cards show the opposite pattern, with fewer yellow cards for dark-skinned players", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["yellow cards"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [143]}, {"id": 145, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[173, 173]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 146, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[174, 174]], "note": "subsection 5.4 heading"}, {"id": 147, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[175, 175]], "assertion": "the sample is limited to European men's soccer, 2012-2013 season, first divisions", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sample scope"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 148, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[176, 176]], "note": "general caveat that results may not generalize elsewhere"}, {"id": 149, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[177, 177]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 150, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[178, 178]], "note": "subsection 5.5 heading"}, {"id": 151, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[179, 179]], "assertion": "the absolute effect (0.17pp on a 1.22% baseline) is described as small (restated)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 152, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[180, 180]], "note": "caveat contrasting statistical vs practical significance"}, {"id": 153, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[181, 181]], "assertion": "for a player with 240 games (sample mean), the estimated difference is about 0.4 red cards over a career", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["individual-level impact"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 154, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[182, 182]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 155, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[183, 183]], "note": "subsection 5.6 heading"}, {"id": 156, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[184, 184]], "assertion": "the primary analysis was pre-specified, but multiple sensitivity analyses were also conducted", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["sensitivity analyses"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 157, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[185, 185]], "note": "caveat about risk of capitalizing on chance"}, {"id": 158, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[186, 186]], "assertion": "the main result is claimed to be robust across specifications, as mitigation for multiple-comparisons risk", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["main result"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 159, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[187, 187]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 160, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[188, 188]], "note": "subsection 5.7 heading"}, {"id": 161, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[189, 189]], "assertion": "standard errors were adjusted for player-level clustering, but referee-level clustering was not addressed", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["standard errors", "clustering"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 162, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[190, 190]], "note": "caveat that dyads may be correlated through shared matches"}, {"id": 163, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[191, 191]], "note": "caveat restating the logistic model's linearity assumption"}, {"id": 164, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[192, 194]], "note": "blank + divider + blank"}, {"id": 165, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[195, 195]], "note": "section 6 heading"}, {"id": 166, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[196, 196]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 167, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[197, 197]], "note": "subsection heading"}, {"id": 168, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[198, 198]], "assertion": "after rigorous adjustment and sensitivity testing, the evidence is said to support a small but statistically significant association between darker skin tone and increased red card probability", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["association"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 169, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[199, 199]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 170, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[200, 200]], "note": "subsection heading"}, {"id": 171, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[201, 201]], "assertion": "the 0.17pp increase is restated as small in absolute terms but a 14% relative increase", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 172, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[202, 202]], "assertion": "over 100 games, a dark-skinned player would expect about 0.14 more red cards than an identical light-skinned player", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["individual-level impact"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 173, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[203, 203]], "assertion": "at the population level (28,896 dark-skinned dyads), the association translates to approximately 49 \"excess\" red cards", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["excess red cards"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 174, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[204, 204]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 175, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[205, 205]], "note": "Mechanisms (Speculation) heading"}, {"id": 176, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[206, 211]], "note": "explicitly labeled speculation about possible mechanisms; no specific action or finding asserted"}, {"id": 177, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[212, 212]], "note": "Alternative Explanations heading"}, {"id": 178, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[213, 217]], "note": "speculative list of alternative explanations for the association"}, {"id": 179, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[218, 218]], "note": "divider"}, {"id": 180, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[219, 222]], "note": "section 7 heading and subsection"}, {"id": 181, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[223, 223]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 182, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[224, 224]], "assertion": "the overall conclusion is stated as SUPPORTED", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["conclusion"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 183, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[225, 225]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 184, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[226, 226]], "assertion": "based on the primary estimand, the hypothesis receives qualified support from the data", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 185, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[227, 228]], "note": "blank + Evidence for support label"}, {"id": 186, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[229, 229]], "assertion": "cited as evidence: the adjusted risk difference of +0.17pp is statistically significant (p=0.027)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 187, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[230, 230]], "assertion": "cited as evidence: the 95% CI [0.05,0.34]pp excludes zero", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confidence interval"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 188, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[231, 231]], "assertion": "cited as evidence: the effect is robust to continuous specification, alternative thresholds, and extreme-groups comparison", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["robustness"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 189, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[232, 232]], "assertion": "cited as evidence: the effect persists after adjustment for key confounders", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confounders"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 190, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[233, 233]], "assertion": "cited as evidence: the direction of the effect is consistent with the hypothesis", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 191, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[234, 235]], "note": "blank + Important caveats label"}, {"id": 192, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[236, 236]], "assertion": "caveat: the effect size is small in absolute terms though non-trivial relatively", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 193, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[237, 237]], "assertion": "caveat: the secondary estimand (odds ratio) is marginally non-significant (p=0.069)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 194, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[238, 238]], "note": "general caveat that observational design precludes causal inference"}, {"id": 195, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[239, 239]], "note": "general caveat about potential unmeasured confounding and selection bias"}, {"id": 196, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[240, 240]], "note": "general caveat that mechanisms remain speculative"}, {"id": 197, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[241, 241]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 198, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[242, 242]], "note": "Statistical Interpretation heading"}, {"id": 199, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[243, 243]], "assertion": "the data are said to provide statistically significant evidence for a positive association between skin tone and red card probability after the stated adjustments, with a small but detectable magnitude given the large sample", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["association", "sample size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 200, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[244, 244]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 201, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[245, 245]], "note": "Substantive Interpretation heading"}, {"id": 202, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[246, 246]], "assertion": "the finding is said to suggest a systematic disparity in red cards by skin tone, consistent with potential implicit bias, though alternative explanations cannot be ruled out", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["disparity", "implicit bias"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 203, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[247, 247]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 204, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[248, 248]], "note": "Final Assessment heading"}, {"id": 205, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[249, 249]], "assertion": "the hypothesis is concluded to be supported by the evidence, with the effect surviving adjustment, significant on the primary estimand, and consistent across robustness checks", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [206]}, {"id": 206, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[249, 249]], "assertion": "the finding is characterized as qualified and said to merit further investigation using experimental or quasi-experimental designs to establish causality", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["future research"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [205]}, {"id": 207, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[250, 252]], "note": "blank + divider + blank"}, {"id": 208, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[253, 253]], "note": "section 8 heading"}, {"id": 209, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[254, 254]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 210, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[255, 260]], "assertion": "all analyses were conducted in Python 3.11 using pandas 1.5.3, numpy 1.24.3, statsmodels 0.14.0, scipy 1.10.1, and matplotlib 3.7.1", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["software", "reproducibility"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 211, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[261, 261]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 212, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[262, 262]], "assertion": "the complete analysis script is provided in final_analysis.py, the random seed was set to 42 for bootstrap reproducibility, and all transformations/specifications/results are documented in the code", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reproducibility", "random seed"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 213, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[263, 263]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 214, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[264, 264]], "assertion": "the data are stated to be available as soccer.csv (33.3MB) in /workspace/data/soccer/", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["data availability"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 215, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[265, 265]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 216, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[266, 266]], "assertion": "the code is stated to be available as final_analysis.py in /workspace/", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["code availability"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 217, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[267, 267]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 218, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[268, 268]], "assertion": "runtime is approximately 3-4 minutes on standard hardware", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["runtime"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 219, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[269, 272]], "note": "blank + divider + blank + Appendix heading"}, {"id": 220, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[273, 273]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 221, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[274, 274]], "note": "Model Specification heading"}, {"id": 222, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[275, 275]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 223, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[276, 279]], "assertion": "the fitted model specification is logit(P(Y=1|X)) = β0 + β1·DarkSkin + β2·Games + β3·YellowCards + β4·Height + β5·Weight + Σβj·Position + Σβk·League", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["model specification"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 224, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[280, 280]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 225, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[281, 284]], "assertion": "in the model Y=1 if any red card in the dyad, DarkSkin=1 if skin tone≥0.5, and standard errors are clustered by player across 1,585 clusters", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["model variables", "clustering"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 226, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[285, 285]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 227, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[286, 286]], "note": "AME Calculation heading"}, {"id": 228, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[287, 287]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 229, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[288, 288]], "assertion": "the average marginal effect was calculated as AME = (1/N)Σᵢ[Φ(Xᵢβ|DarkSkin=1) − Φ(Xᵢβ|DarkSkin=0)]", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["average marginal effects"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 230, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[289, 289]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 231, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "background", "lines": [[290, 290]], "note": "definition of Φ as the logistic CDF, not tied to a choice"}, {"id": 232, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[291, 291]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 233, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[292, 292]], "note": "Bootstrap Procedure heading"}, {"id": 234, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[293, 293]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 235, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[294, 299]], "assertion": "the bootstrap procedure resampled players with replacement, included all dyads for sampled players, fit logistic regression, calculated AME, repeated 200 times, and computed percentile CIs (2.5%, 97.5%)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["bootstrap procedure"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 236, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[300, 300]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 237, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[301, 301]], "assertion": "this bootstrap procedure is claimed to account for within-player correlation while maintaining the dyadic structure", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["bootstrap procedure"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}]}}